---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import RecordChain from "../components/RecordChain.astro";
import HubStack from "../components/HubStack.astro";
import { href, ext } from "../lib/site";
---
<Layout>
  <!-- Hero: who it is for, the two promises, one primary action -->
  <section class="section hero">
    <div class="wrap hero__grid">
      <div class="hero__copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">For schools &amp; educational organisations</p>
        <h1 class="hero__h">
          <span>Reduce administrative load.</span>
          <span class="hero__h2">Enhance and extend learning.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="lede">We take on the administrative work — accounting, contracts and the recurring tasks around them — alongside the system you already use. And we bring learning modules into the classroom, online or on site. Both leave a sealed record.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn" href={href("/request-access/")}>Request pilot access</a>
          <a class="link" href={href("/modules/#available")}>Try the first module</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="hero__facts" aria-label="Status">
          <li><span class="chip chip--built">Sealed record · built</span></li>
          <li><span class="chip chip--dev">Engine · in development</span></li>
          <li class="mono small muted">Swiss/EU data residency · AGPL-3.0</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="hero__demo">
        <RecordChain />
        <p class="small muted hero__demonote">In the Hub, every finished step writes one line like these, sealed against the one before it. Anyone holding the log can re-compute the chain without our help.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What we do: two services on one foundation -->
  <section class="section" id="what">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">What we do</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Two services: the back office and the classroom.</h2>
      <p class="intro">Both come in formats adapted to your needs. You can implement and self-host the tools and modules yourself; otherwise we guide, implement, host and maintain them for you.</p>
      <div class="grid grid--2">
        <article class="card card--link">
          <div class="card__head"><h3>The back office</h3><span class="chip">as an engagement</span></div>
          <p class="for">for the work nobody went into education to do</p>
          <p>Accounting, contracts and the recurring administration around them, taken on with you and against the system you already run, whether that is CashCtrl, bexio or another. Scoped per organisation as a pilot. Decisions stay with your people; we do the work around them.</p>
          <a class="link" href={href("/service/")}>Back-office tooling</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card card--link">
          <div class="card__head"><h3>Learning modules</h3><span class="chip chip--live">online &amp; on site</span></div>
          <p class="for">for a class, a family, or a single student</p>
          <p>Scoped and built on request by contributors in social work, nature-based and technical fields, matched to the age and size of the class. Delivered online, at your site, or both, with materials, transport and evaluation included where desired.</p>
          <a class="link" href={href("/modules/")}>See the modules</a>
        </article>
      </div>
      <article class="card foundation">
        <div class="foundation__k">
          <div class="card__head"><h3>A record underneath both</h3><span class="chip chip--built">built</span></div>
          <p class="for">for the question “who changed this, and when?”</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>Whatever we touch leaves an entry in a sealed log: what happened, who did it, in what order. You can show it to a parent, a board or an auditor, and they can check it without taking our word for it.</p>
          <a class="link" href={href("/roadmap/")}>What is built, and what is not</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How we work -->
  <section class="section band" id="how">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Built from the ground up, not configured.</h2>
      <p class="human">Most solutions for educational organisations can only be configured.</p>
      <p class="human small">entrosana opens the room to decide what you need from the ground up: no tools full of functions nobody uses, and no learning tasks designed for repetitive mass learning.</p>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <h3>Tell us what you envision</h3>
          <p>Map out your specific needs, intended solutions and known obstacles. We take your instructions into account while we build your solution.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Review our suggestions</h3>
          <p>This is the time to make room for process optimisations, potential automations and mapping out the implementation.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Progressive adaptation</h3>
          <p>For us an implementation is never finished: the use case may stay while the options change, or the other way around. Want to maintain a solution yourself? Get in touch.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Hub + how data is handled -->
  <section class="section" id="hub">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">One ground. What stands on it.</p>
        <h2 class="h2">The Hub, and what runs in it.</h2>
        <p>The Hub is the ground: shared identity, one sealed record, one licence. Tools run the back office on it; modules run in the classroom on it. Both leave the same trail, so what happened can be shown rather than asserted.</p>
        <p>Students, parents and teachers work alongside outside contributors, in the open under AGPL-3.0. The Hub is being built at <a href={ext.hub}><b>entrosana.app</b></a>.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn btn--hub" href={ext.hub}>Access entrosana Hub →</a>
          <a class="link" href={href("/hub/")}>Learn about the Hub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hub__fig">
        <HubStack />
        <div class="datanote">
          <p class="tag">How data is handled</p>
          <p><strong>Two model layers, by design.</strong> Delicate records are designed to stay on a model served on your hardware or ours; only data that is not sensitive may go to an online provider. In development alongside the engine.</p>
          <a class="link" href={href("/service/#data")}>See the data boundary</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Where we stand -->
  <section class="section band" id="status">
    <div class="wrap split split--wide-left">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Where we stand</p>
        <h2 class="h2">In development. In the open.</h2>
        <p>entrosana is in development, and we say so wherever it matters. The engine behind the back-office tools is public under AGPL-3.0 and is not production software today. No school runs on the engine yet, and modules are delivered by people rather than by software. Pilot access is opening to a small group of Swiss organisations.</p>
        <p>The aim is systemic: an open service any school and any back office can inherit. To see current prototypes, open the Arboro showcase, developed for our first collaboration partner.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn" href={href("/request-access/")}>Request pilot access</a>
          <a class="link" href={href("/roadmap/")}>Read the roadmap</a>
          <a class="link" href={ext.arboro}>Arboro showcase</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <ul class="status-list" aria-label="Status by part">
          <li><span class="what">Audit trail</span><span class="chip chip--built">built</span></li>
          <li><span class="what">Sign-in &amp; separation</span><span class="chip chip--built">built</span></li>
          <li><span class="what">Back-office workflows</span><span class="chip chip--dev">in development</span></li>
          <li><span class="what">Modules</span><span class="chip chip--live">available · by people</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="small muted founder">Founded by Gianluca Kühne. Source: <a href={ext.source}>github.com/entrosana/hub</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: clamp(2rem, 1rem + 4vw, 4.5rem); }
  .hero__grid { display: grid; gap: clamp(2rem, 1rem + 4vw, 3.5rem); align-items: center; }
  @media (min-width: 980px) { .hero__grid { grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr; } }
  /* hero headline as live: two lines, one ink, weight carries the hierarchy (600 → 350) */
  .hero__h {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 1.8rem + 2.4vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -.028em;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: .4rem 0 3rem;
  }
  .hero__h span { display: block; }
  .hero__h2 { font-weight: 350; color: var(--ink); margin-top: 1.4rem; }
  @media (min-width: 1000px) {
    .hero__h { font-size: clamp(2rem, .9rem + 2.6vw, 3.6rem); line-height: 1.08; margin: 0 0 1.6rem; }
    .hero__h2 { margin-top: 0; }
  }
  .hero__facts { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem 0.75rem; margin-top: 1.75rem; }
  .hero__demonote { margin-top: 0.75rem; max-width: 52ch; }

  .foundation { margin-top: clamp(1rem, 0.6rem + 1.5vw, 1.5rem); display: grid; gap: 0.5rem 2rem; border-style: dashed; border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--verify) 50%, var(--line)); }
  @media (min-width: 820px) { .foundation { grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr; } }
  .foundation .link { margin-top: 0.5rem; }

  .hub__fig { display: grid; gap: 1.25rem; }
  .datanote { padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--seal); background: var(--surface); border-radius: 0 var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0; }
  .datanote p { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .datanote .tag { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }

  .founder { margin-top: 1.25rem; }
</style>
